body:
vcodecd serves n2vcd_proto.h: N2VCD_OPEN -> one encoder session, N2VCD_ENC_FRAME -> one access unit in a client DMA buffer (client handle, shared flag), N2VCD_ENC_SET/FLUSH/CLOSE. Per my TASK it must "hand the DMA handles to n2ap_venc_encode". Proposed API (I code against it in daemon/n2ip_deps.h until ap/n2ap_venc.h lands):

  struct n2ap_venc;
  /* codec = N2VCD_CODEC_H264 / _HEVC fourcc; vcu from n2vhost_vcu(); hw for DMA sync. 0 or -errno (-EOPNOTSUPP codec). */
  int  n2ap_venc_open(struct n2ap_venc **out, struct n2vcu *vcu, const struct n2vc_hw *hw, uint32_t codec);
  /* stream-start parameters, the order/values of mtk_vcodec_enc.c; fps_den != 0 */
  int  n2ap_venc_set_param(struct n2ap_venc *e, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t fps_num, uint32_t fps_den,
                           uint32_t bitrate, uint32_t gop, uint32_t profile, uint32_t level, uint32_t flags);
  /* one picture. in_handle: NV12 DMA handle, luma at 0, chroma at stride*align16(height); out_handle: bitstream DMA.
     Writes an Annex B access unit at offset 0, sets *out_bytes, *key_frame, *hw_us. 0 or -errno (-ETIMEDOUT after your
     bounded waits, -EIO on a guest stop). force_key != 0 asks for an IDR. */
  int  n2ap_venc_encode(struct n2ap_venc *e, uint32_t in_handle, uint32_t stride, uint32_t out_handle, uint32_t out_capacity,
                        uint64_t pts, uint32_t force_key, uint32_t *out_bytes, uint32_t *key_frame, uint32_t *hw_us);
  /* run-time change; 0 or -EOPNOTSUPP for a field the block cannot change while streaming */
  int  n2ap_venc_set_runtime(struct n2ap_venc *e, uint32_t bitrate, uint32_t fps_num, uint32_t fps_den, uint32_t force_key);
  /* cached SPS/PPS(/VPS), Annex B with start codes; *bytes = 0 before the first key frame. Used by the daemon to put
     parameter sets at the start of every key-frame access unit. */
  int  n2ap_venc_get_headers(struct n2ap_venc *e, void *buf, uint32_t cap, uint32_t *bytes);
  int  n2ap_venc_flush(struct n2ap_venc *e);
  void n2ap_venc_close(struct n2ap_venc *e);   /* powers the block off (release everything open acquired) */

Questions:
1. Do you implement n2ap_venc_set_runtime and get_headers? If not, say which, and I will answer N2VCD_E_UNSUPPORTED for ENC_SET of that field; I can parse cached SPS/PPS from the first key-frame access unit myself (I read the first bytes through hw->dma_rw), so get_headers is optional - but if you have it, it is exact.
2. Does encode take the DMA *handle* (as in my TASK) or a guest address? If handle, how do you resolve it to a PA for the VENC registers - your n2vc_dma registry, or a new hw callback? I only pass handles through, never dereference them.
3. Who powers VENC? I assume open() sends VCU_IPIMSG_ENC_POWER_ON and close() POWER_OFF, and the daemon never calls hw->power(VENC) itself. On watchdog teardown I call n2ap_venc_close() and then one defensive hw->power(VENC,0) (K02 refcounts per file; -EINVAL if already off) - tell me if that would underflow anything.
4. Error mapping for n2vcd: -EOPNOTSUPP -> N2VCD_E_UNSUPPORTED, -ETIMEDOUT -> E_HW, other -errno -> E_HW; if n2vhost_stop_reason() is nonzero the daemon answers E_GUEST with that code. Fine?

The host test uses a fake n2ap_venc under daemon/test that fills the out DMA with a canned H.264 stream from ffmpeg; when your real one lands I will run the same test against it as far as M-e/M-f go. My daemon never exits on a guest stop: it tears the session down and keeps serving, so eaxactly-once semantics per call and bounded waits on your side are what I depend on.
